# Mail account the sweep sends email applications from (scripts/mail.mjs). Copy this file to
# .mail.env in your workspace and fill in MAIL_USER; it is the address the mail goes out from, and the
# script refuses to guess it.
#
# macOS and Windows, no password needed (the default there). Many Google accounts no longer offer
# app passwords, so this path comes first. The script hands the mail to the mail app on this machine:
#   macOS: Mail.app. Add the account in System Settings > Internet Accounts, open Mail once, and allow
#          the terminal (or Claude) to control Mail when macOS asks.
#   Windows: classic Outlook with the account added. The new Outlook has no scripting interface, so
#          it does not work; use SMTP there. (This path is untested.)
MAIL_USER=you@gmail.com
MAIL_FROM_NAME=First Last
#
# SMTP, any OS, with an app password. Setting MAIL_APP_PASSWORD makes SMTP the default; then run
# chmod 600 .mail.env. The app password: Google account with 2-step verification on, open
# https://myaccount.google.com/apppasswords, create one named "autopilot-jobsearch" and copy the
# 16 characters without the spaces. It is not your account password, and you can revoke it there.
# MAIL_APP_PASSWORD=xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
# For an account that is not Gmail, set the provider's SMTP host and TLS port:
# MAIL_HOST=smtp.gmail.com
# MAIL_PORT=465
#
# Optional: force a transport instead of the default above (smtp, applemail or outlook).
# MAIL_TRANSPORT=applemail
